; Modular ERB: Addition/Custom_Commands/Add_CUSTOM_COM18 Commission.ERB
;Commissions are projects which can be undertaken by characters at the player's behest to grant benefits or create changes in the game world.
;Each commission has its own associated cost in funds, time, and specific items.
;There are also random events that may slow the commission's progress or require additional items or funds to continue, or speed it up.
;Only specific characters can begin a commission, with the individual characters being specific to that work. Only one character can take a given commission at a time.
;Some characters might have special properties that affect how the work progresses.
;Brief overview of ideas for themes and quirks for specific characters:
;Tewi - Enhancements and miscellaneous services. Cheap and fast compared to other characters, but with a high rate of potentially expensive bad events.
;Minoriko - Lucrative food-related commissions only available in fall.
;Nitori - Focused on construction and excavation. Very stable and "normal" for jobs that last four days or less, and has positive events, but longer jobs gain a very high rate of bad events.
;Takane - Same jobs as Nitori, but slower and more expensive in exchange for greater stability.
;Yamame - Construction. Extremely fast, but high stall rate and requires medicinal herbs and the like to resolve issues (treating disease).
;Sumireko - Errands involving the outside world. High event rate, good and bad, with highly random outcomes.
;Tsukasa - Social engineering, such as temporarily raising acceptance values or making it easier to remove hate marks. Only takes Charisma, no material costs.
;Momoyo - Excavation and the like. Fast work without problems, but requires extra rare materials such as dragon gems.
;Yumemi - Wacky high-tech stuff. Extremely expensive, might require rare materials, but very stable.
;Below here are some example functions that can be adapted by dialogues.
;To add a new commission, or to allow a character to be hired for one, use these functions. These can be defined in KOJO files.
;Each commission needs a unique number between 1 and COMMISSION_MAX. They don't need to be strictly sequential, so they can be added and removed as necessary.
;These examples create a commission for delivering ingredients that can be accessed by any character with a COMMISSION_ABLE_1_{ID} function in their dialogue.
;Checking functions with modular names aren't #FUNCTIONs because we can only call them on their own lines and check RESULT.

@COMMISSION_NAME_1
;Checks the given commission's name.
RESULTS = Deliver ingredients
RETURN 1

@COMMISSION_COST_1(ARG)
;Returns an item and quantity thereof in the commission's requirements.
;ARG is which item slot the item is in on the cost list when viewing the commission. These start from 1 and must be sequential, but there can be as many as you want.
;You can also overwrite the default cost in a character's dialogue by adding the character's ID at the end of the function and using the same ARG. See Tewi's cost function below.
;The necessary quantity of the item is returned as RESULT:1.
SELECTCASE ARG
	;Each CASE here is one pair of item and quantity. You can add as many CASEs as you want.
	CASE 0
		;The item's quantity.
		RESULT:1 = 25000
		;The item's ID. You can also return -1 for nothing, -2 for a rotor, -3 for yen, -4 for Charisma, or -5 for lumber.
		RETURN -3
ENDSELECT

@COMMISSION_RESOLUTION_COST_1(ARG)
;Returns an item and quantity thereof in the commission's resolution requirements. Not required.
;When a commission is stalled by an event, the issue can be resolved by paying this cost through the commission menu.
;If no cost is given (by not defining this function or by returning 0 on the first case), the commission can never be manually resolved if stalled, and must be resolved through events.
;All parameters for this function are the same as the regular cost function. You can make character-specific functions like the regular one, as well.
SELECTCASE ARG
	CASE 0
		RESULT:1 = 500
		RETURN -3
ENDSELECT

@COMMISSION_RATE_1
;Returns the default rate of progress for the given commission.
;1000 progress or more equals completion, so a rate of 500 means it will be done after two days.
RETURN 500
;The below functions are defined in Tewi's dialogue, but are duplicated here for ease of reference. These are the only ones you need to copy if you just want to add a character to a commission.
;Commission assignments are on a per dialogue basis. If an alternate dialogue has an identifier, it goes after the ID in the function name, for example K51_EGG.
;Below are the core functions that manage the commission system.

@ADD_CUSTOM_COM18
CALL SET_KOJO_COLOR(TARGET)
CALL COMMISSION_CHARACTER_MENU(TARGET)
RESETCOLOR
RETURN -1

@ADD_CUSTOM_COM_ABLE18
;Check to see if the commission command can be used. The target character must be either working on a commission or capable of taking one.
#DIMS DYNAMIC CharacterID
SIF !TARGET
	RETURN 0
SIF !TFLAG:100
	RETURN 0
SIF !SHIRAHU(TARGET)
	RETURN 0
SIF CFLAG:MASTER:うふふ
	RETURN 0
CharacterID '= @"{TARGET}"
;Check if the character is using an alternate dialogue, and if so, get its identifier.
IF CFLAG:TARGET:口上セレクタ
	RESULTS =
	TRYCALLFORM M_KOJO_K{TARGET}_{CFLAG:TARGET:口上セレクタ}
	CharacterID '= @"{TARGET}%RESULTS%"
ENDIF
FOR LOCAL,1,COMMISSION_MAX
;Loop through every commission and check to see if the character can take it or is currently working on it.
RESULT = 0
TRYCALLFORM COMMISSION_ABLE_{LOCAL}_K%CharacterID%
IF (RESULT || COMMISSION_PROGRESS:LOCAL) && COMMISSION_PROGRESS:LOCAL < 1000 && (!COMMISSION_PROGRESS:LOCAL || COMMISSION_CHARACTER:LOCAL == TARGET)
	;Return true if any commission is valid.
	RETURN 1
ENDIF
NEXT
RETURN 0

@COMMISSION_CURRENT(Character)
;Checks what commission the given character is currently undertaking, if any.
#FUNCTION
#DIM DYNAMIC Character
FOR LOCAL,1,COMMISSION_MAX
;Loop through every commission and check to see if it's in progress and assigned to the character.
IF COMMISSION_CHARACTER:LOCAL == Character && COMMISSION_PROGRESS:LOCAL && COMMISSION_PROGRESS:LOCAL < 1000
	RETURNF LOCAL
ENDIF
NEXT
RETURNF 0

@COMMISSION_CHARACTER_MENU(Character)
;The main commissions menu, which can be accessed from any character that has a commission available.
#DIM DYNAMIC Character
#DIM DYNAMIC Commission
#DIMS DYNAMIC CharacterID
$TOP
LOCALS =
;Set the character's portrait to angry, blushing, or happy as appropriate.
IF MARK:Character:反発刻印 || CFLAG:Character:ブチギレ
	LOCALS = 怒り
ELSEIF (TCVAR:Character:媚薬 || TCVAR:Character:発情) && LS_ACTIVE() == ""
	LOCALS = 発情
ELSEIF TALENT:Character:機嫌 > 0
	LOCALS = 笑顔
ENDIF
Commission = COMMISSION_CURRENT(Character)
CharacterID '= @"{Character}"
;Check if the character is using an alternate dialogue, and if so, get its identifier.
IF CFLAG:Character:口上セレクタ
	RESULTS =
	TRYCALLFORM M_KOJO_K{Character}_{CFLAG:Character:口上セレクタ}
	CharacterID '= @"{Character}%RESULTS%"
ENDIF
PRINTL
CALL PRINT_FACE(Character,LOCALS,"服",,COND_STR("照れ",LS_ACTIVE() != ""))
RESULT = 0
;Call the character's status print function.
TRYCALLFORM COMMISSION_STATUS_K%CharacterID%
CALL D_LINE
PRINTFORMDL
IF Commission
	;If a commission is underway.
	RESULTS = 알 수 없는 의뢰
	TRYCALLFORM COMMISSION_NAME_{Commission}
	PRINTFORMDL %RESULTS%
	LOCAL = COMMISSION_PROGRESS:Commission
	SIF LOCAL < 0
		LOCAL *= -1
	CALL PRINT_COLORBAR(LOCAL,1000,20,UNICODE(0x2584),UNICODE(0x2584),0xC0C0C0,0x404040)
	PRINTFORMDL
	PRINTFORMD 상태: 
	;Print the status of the commission based on its expected progress compared with its actual progress.
	IF COMMISSION_PROGRESS:Commission < 0
		CALL COLORMESSAGE(@"정체됨",C_RED,1)
		RESULT = 0
		TRYCALLFORM COMMISSION_RESOLUTION_COST_{Commission}(0)
		IF !RESULT
			CALL COLORMESSAGE(@"수동으로 해결할 수 없다.",C_RED,1)
		ELSE
			PRINTFORMDL
			PRINTFORMDL 문제를 해결하기 위해 제공할 것:
			PRINTFORMDL
			LOCAL:1 = 0
			WHILE 1
			;Loop through function definitions for the commission's requirements until they run out.
			RESULT = 0
			TRYCALLFORM COMMISSION_RESOLUTION_COST_{Commission}_K%CharacterID%(LOCAL:1)
			LOCAL:2 = RESULT
			LOCAL:3 = RESULT:1
			IF !LOCAL:2
				;If there's no dialogue-specific cost in the slot, check the default.
				TRYCALLFORM COMMISSION_RESOLUTION_COST_{Commission}(LOCAL:1)
				LOCAL:2 = RESULT
				LOCAL:3 = RESULT:1
			ENDIF
			SELECTCASE LOCAL:2
				CASE 0
					;No requirement.
					BREAK
				CASE -1
					;Nothing.
					;This is used by dialogues to remove default requirements, so we skip it and move on to the next loop.
				CASE -2
					;Rotor.
					PRINTFORMDL %@"%三桁区切(LOCAL:3)% %PLURALIZER(ITEMNAME_TR(0),LOCAL:3)%", 20, LEFT% %@"(On hand: %三桁区切(ITEM:0)%)", 3, RIGHT%
				CASE -3
					;Yen.
					PRINTFORMDL %@"%金額表示(LOCAL:3)%", 20, LEFT% %@"(On hand: %金額表示(MONEY)%)", 3, RIGHT%
				CASE -4
					;Charisma.
					PRINTFORMDL %@"%三桁区切(LOCAL:3)%CM", 20, LEFT% %@"(On hand: %三桁区切(MONEY:2)%CM)", 3, RIGHT%
				CASE -5
					;Lumber.
					LOCAL:4 = 0
					LOCAL:5 = 0
					FOR LOCAL:6, 1, 13
					LOCAL:4 = MIN(LOCAL:4+LOG_SALES:(LOCAL:6),LOCAL:3)
					LOCAL:5 += LOG_SALES:(LOCAL:6)
					NEXT
					PRINTFORMDL %@"%三桁区切(LOCAL:3)% lumber", 20, LEFT% %@"(On hand: %三桁区切(LOCAL:5)%)", 3, RIGHT%
				CASEELSE
					;Any other item.
					PRINTFORMDL %@"%三桁区切(LOCAL:3)% %PLURALIZER(ITEMNAME_TR(LOCAL:2),LOCAL:3)%", 20, LEFT% %@"(On hand: %三桁区切(ITEM:(LOCAL:2))%)", 3, RIGHT%
			ENDSELECT
			LOCAL:1++
			WEND
			PRINTFORMDL
			PRINTFORMDL [0] 해결하기
			PRINTFORMDL [1] 의뢰 취소
			PRINTFORMDL [2] 돌아가기
			$LOOP
			INPUT
			SELECTCASE RESULT
				CASE 0
					CALL COMMISSION_PURCHASE(Commission,Character,1)
					IF !RESULT
						PRINTFORMDW 너는 그것을 감당할 수 없어.
